---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Grid from '../../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import Story from '../../components/Story.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="During a Storm"
  description="Evacuation and transportation assistance, pet-friendly emergency lodging, connectivity, and a storm support hotline."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="During a storm"
    title="When leaving is the right call but not a simple one"
    lede="Evacuation orders assume you have a car, somewhere to go, and nobody with you who complicates the trip. For a lot of families, none of that is true."
  />

  <Section>
    <p class="urgent">
      <strong>If you are in immediate danger, call 911.</strong> Our hotline is a
      non-emergency service.
    </p>
    <Grid>
      <Card title="Emergency lodging" meta="Pets welcome">
        <p>
          Through hotel partnerships we place families in safe rooms ahead of
          landfall. Before Milton we secured discounted Hilton rooms in Orlando
          with breakfast and parking included, and placed more than 20 people.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Pets come too.</strong> That is not an exception we make; it is the point.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Evacuation & transportation" meta="Including if you have no car">
        <p>
          If you have nowhere to go or no way to get there, we arrange it. For one
          family that meant coordinating an unusually complicated ride for two
          adults, two kids, two cats and a dog, over a hundred miles inland.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Storm support hotline" meta="Non-emergency">
        <p>
          Real-time forecasts, radar, shelter status, and answers to the specific
          questions official hotlines can't take: what your zone means for you,
          what to do about a cracked window, how to keep power to medical
          equipment if you're staying.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Staying connected" meta="Free">
        <p>
          During Milton we provided free one-month unlimited talk and text plans
          for eSIM-compatible phones, so families cut off from service could still
          reach each other.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="The questions we actually get">
    <p class="lede-inline">
      These came into the hotline during the 2024 storms. Not one of them has a
      useful answer on a government website.
    </p>
    <ul class="quotes">
      <li>“Can I still leave if I'm in Zone B?”</li>
      <li>“My window is cracked. What do I do?”</li>
      <li>“My daughter's on a ventilator, and I'm staying. How can I keep the power on?”</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Official guidance told one caller to seek a local public shelter. The
      nearest one was thirty miles away and she had no car. Being technically
      correct is not the same as being useful.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Peter's story">
    <Story name="Peter" context="Hurricane Milton · emergency lodging">
      <p>
        Forced to leave their dorm ahead of Milton, Peter had no family nearby to
        call. The shelters wouldn't take their cat — their only companion. When
        they contacted us, they said they were planning to ride out the storm in
        their car.
      </p>
      <p>We could not let that happen. Through our Hilton partnership we placed
        Peter and their cat in a safe hotel the same day.</p>
      <blockquote>
        Wonderful, wonderful people. My cat and I have only been able to safely
        make it through Hurricane Milton because of the help given to us by this
        organization. I cannot convey enough how above and beyond they've gone in
        ensuring our safety.
      </blockquote>
    </Story>
    <p class="more"><a class="btn" href="/help/request">Request assistance</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .urgent {
    background: rgba(215, 38, 56, 0.08);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--flp-red-500);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .lede-inline { font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .quotes { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--space-md) 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-sm); }
  .quotes li {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .more { margin-top: var(--space-md); }
</style>
